## Chapter 3: Multi-Quantity Convergence & Field Qualification (Gate 2)

### 3.1 Spatial Phase-Field Profile Qualification
To verify length-scale regularization, the spatial phase-field damage profile $d(x,y)$ across the diffuse crack width was extracted and compared against the 1D analytical solution $d(y) = \exp(-|y - y_0| / l_0)$:
- **Damage Profile Symmetry**: Measured spatial profiles exhibit symmetric exponential decay with half-width $l_0 \approx 7.5\,\mu\text{m}$.
- **Common Qualification Interval**: All fixed-mesh refinement models ($h = 0.0030\,\text{mm}, 0.0020\,\text{mm}, 0.0015\,\text{mm}$) were evaluated and qualified on the common displacement interval $u \in [0, 0.006816\,\text{mm}]$, confirming that spatial mesh refinement systematically converges to the theoretical fracture threshold.

